---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Us - ${siteConfig.name} | Cinema Journalism & Editorial Standards`}
  description="Learn about TG Movies, our founder Aman Alria, editorial independence, review methodology, and our commitment to verified cinema journalism."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 mb-2">
        <span>Editorial Standards & Masthead</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        About TG Movies
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">
        Independent cinema analysis, verified theatrical box office tracking, and curated OTT streaming coverage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-6">
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">
        Welcome to <strong>TG Movies</strong> (accessible at <a href="https://tgmovies.in" class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">tgmovies.in</a>), a premier independent film publication dedicated to delivering authentic movie critiques, data-backed box office analysis, streaming breakdowns, and cinema industry journalism. Founded and directed by <strong>Aman Alria</strong>, TG Movies was created to bridge the critical gap between clickbait rumor mills and rigorous, data-verified entertainment reporting.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Our Editorial Mission & Foundation
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        The cinematic landscape moves at breakneck velocity. In an era dominated by instantaneous social media reactions, synthetic fan theories, and unverified studio leaks, modern audiences require clarity and integrity. TG Movies was established on three non-negotiable principles: uncompromising factual veracity, deep narrative literacy, and transparent methodology. We do not recycle anonymous forum rumors or publish unverified claims. Every theatrical release date, box office milestone, producer statement, and casting report published across our platform undergoes strict primary-source validation against verified trade agencies, official studio announcements, and registered distributor records.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Whether examining a massive multiversal Hollywood tentpole such as <em>Spider-Man: Brand New Day</em> or tracking domestic box office earnings across Indian cinema including Bollywood, South Cinema, and regional industries, our analysis treats cinema both as an artistic craft and a global economic ecosystem.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Editorial Leadership & Author Profile
      </h2>
      <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50/50 dark:bg-slate-900/50">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4 mb-4">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-sky-600 text-white font-extrabold text-2xl flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            A
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Aman Alria</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
              Chief Editor & Film Journalist
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono mt-0.5">
              Direct Contact: amanalha07@gmail.com
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Aman Alria oversees all editorial operations, publication workflows, investigative reporting, and critical evaluations across TG Movies. With extensive background tracking domestic and international entertainment markets, film production pipelines, and streaming economics, Aman provides readers with authoritative perspectives grounded in objective industry realities rather than sensationalism.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Our Critical Review Methodology
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Our movie critiques and streaming assessments follow a structured, multi-dimensional evaluation rubric that separates artistic achievement from personal bias:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <li><strong>Narrative Architecture & Screenplay Integrity:</strong> We analyze structural pacing, thematic resonance, character arcs, exposition management, and logical continuity rather than simple plot synopsis summaries.</li>
        <li><strong>Directorial Vision & Technical Craftsmanship:</strong> We assess cinematographic framing, color grading, lighting choices, editorial rhythm, practical versus digital visual effects (VFX), and spatial staging.</li>
        <li><strong>Performance Dynamics:</strong> We evaluate ensemble chemistry, character dedication, vocal modulation, and dramatic authenticity across lead and supporting casts.</li>
        <li><strong>Sound Design & Acoustic Scoring:</strong> We review original thematic scores, ambient mixing, and audio balance to understand how acoustic craft shapes emotional impact.</li>
        <li><strong>Cultural & Genre Context:</strong> We evaluate how a film functions within its respective genre, honoring foundational traditions while acknowledging genuine creative innovation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Box Office Tracking & Financial Analytics
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Financial reporting at TG Movies strictly avoids speculative numbers. Our box office team cross-references theatrical receipts against accredited industry tracking services, including Sacnilk, Bollywood Hungama, Comscore, Box Office Mojo, distributor press notices, and national cinema chain returns (PVR INOX, Cinepolis). When reporting Indian box office numbers, we explicitly differentiate between Net Box Office Collection (NBOC) and Gross Worldwide figures to provide transparent, unambiguous financial clarity.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Commitment to Zero Misinformation & Corrections Policy
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Accuracy is our foremost responsibility. In the rare event that an error of fact occurs—whether regarding an official release date adjustment, a revised box office tally, or an executive production attribution—we issue clear, timestamped corrections at the top of the relevant article. We invite our readership to report any factual inaccuracies directly to our editorial inbox at <a href="mailto:amanalha07@gmail.com" class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">amanalha07@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Editorial Independence & Commercial Transparency
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        TG Movies maintains total editorial independence. We do not accept paid reviews, paid promotional praise, or sponsored critiques. Advertisements displayed on this site via Google AdSense or authorized network partners are strictly separated from our editorial assessments. No studio, producer, streaming network, or marketing agency exercises influence or preview approval over any review, rating, or investigative article published by our journalists.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
